<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Reboot (250)</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>reboot              (in 1 minute)
reboot &lt;minutes&gt;    (for example: reboot 30)
reboot now
reboot cancel
</pre>
<p>Reboots the game: the server stops, and the script that keeps it running 
(runvme.sh) starts it again. Players are saved and must log in again.
</p><p>The players are warned: when the reboot is set, if it is less than 20 
minutes away; then at 10 and 5 minutes, at 30 and 10 seconds, and with 
"Rebooting...". A reboot set further off than 20 minutes is announced 
only from 10 minutes on.
</p><p>Only one reboot can be pending: reboot cancel stops it, and tells the 
players "The reboot has been halted.". reboot now reboots at once, 
without warning. It is logged.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Shutdown</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Broadcast</a>
</pre>




</div>